WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.109
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:24.379 --> 00:28.716
NIGHT SHIFT WORKERS MUST WORK IN PAIRS, AND UNAUTHORIZED DEPARTURE IS PROHIBITED

3
00:40.770 --> 00:45.692
DO NOT ENTER THE STORAGE ROOM IF YOU HEAR ANY NOISES INSIDE

4
00:46.818 --> 00:51.489
USE THE CROSS IN THE STORAGE ROOM TO DEAL WITH NON-HUMAN ENTITIES

5
00:53.783 --> 00:58.329
RULE VIOLATIONS RESULT IN TERMINATION OF PART-TIME JOB AND SEVERE PENALTIES

6
01:01.249 --> 01:02.917
It's a bright Monday morning.

7
01:03.001 --> 01:05.461
The perfect time to get out there and make some money, folks.

8
01:05.545 --> 01:07.755
Today, we start with a story from "King of Gigs."

9
01:07.839 --> 01:10.049
"I was scammed by a crooked landlord,

10
01:10.133 --> 01:13.219
and now I'm trying to cover up that I'm over a million won in debt."

11
01:13.303 --> 01:16.014
"Lease terms seemed too good to be true. Who can I blame but myself?"

12
01:16.097 --> 01:17.432
"I have no hope."

13
01:18.099 --> 01:19.851
MR. BYEON HYEOK-JUN, YOUR LOAN INTEREST IS DUE

14
01:19.934 --> 01:21.978
PRINCIPAL: 140 MILLION WON INTEREST DUE: 4 MILLION WON

15
01:23.062 --> 01:24.022
Oh, shit.

16
01:35.325 --> 01:36.910
HOUSING SCAM VICTIM PROGRAM: NOT SELECTED

17
01:36.993 --> 01:39.245
CREDIT RATING DROP PAST DUE, PAYMENT DUE

18
01:41.789 --> 01:43.291
Shit, I'm not doing this.

19
01:53.134 --> 01:54.010
Mom.

20
01:56.804 --> 01:58.139
Ji-yoon.

21
02:01.017 --> 02:02.435
I'm sorry, everyone.

22
02:05.396 --> 02:06.439
Goodbye.

23
02:13.279 --> 02:14.197
Oh sh…

24
02:24.791 --> 02:26.793
ULTRA-HIGH DAILY WAGE PART-TIME JOBS

25
02:29.671 --> 02:31.464
ULTRA-HIGH DAILY WAGE SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

26
02:31.547 --> 02:33.800
"A last-minute second chance?"

27
03:33.818 --> 03:35.194
DEAD-END JOB

28
03:38.323 --> 03:41.326
CONVENIENCE STORE RULES

29
03:55.631 --> 03:57.592
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

30
03:57.675 --> 03:59.761
"Spider Staffing Agency?"

31
04:00.553 --> 04:02.722
Aren't these agencies for worker ants?

32
04:02.805 --> 04:03.931
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

33
04:37.799 --> 04:39.217
Hey, is anyone here?

34
04:54.399 --> 04:55.566
What the hell?

35
05:05.493 --> 05:06.661
You looking for work?

36
05:06.744 --> 05:08.204
Oh. Yeah.

37
05:08.287 --> 05:09.414
Have a seat.

38
05:12.750 --> 05:15.086
So, is this really a high-paying opportunity?

39
05:15.169 --> 05:16.712
I have a lot of debt I need to pay off,

40
05:16.796 --> 05:19.632
so I'm willing to do anything, but nothing illegal.

41
05:19.715 --> 05:20.675
Ah.

42
05:22.051 --> 05:24.929
So the pay… Here's how we structure it.

43
05:25.012 --> 05:27.682
We count in multiples of the minimum wage,

44
05:28.891 --> 05:31.352
so the pay starts off at ten times the base wage.

45
05:31.853 --> 05:34.439
And you'll get paid for the work on the day that you complete it.

46
05:34.522 --> 05:37.233
Any openings right now? Jobs I could start soon?

47
05:37.316 --> 05:38.943
I'd be ready right now.

48
05:39.986 --> 05:44.699
Immediate openings? Let's just take a look.

49
05:46.325 --> 05:49.579
What do we have on the schedule today? Let me see.

50
05:49.662 --> 05:52.707
This is your first time here. You've got a fairly sturdy build.

51
05:52.790 --> 05:54.500
What is something you could start right away?

52
05:54.584 --> 05:56.627
Oh, this one's 50 times the standard rate.

53
05:57.462 --> 05:58.629
Wait a minute.

54
05:58.713 --> 06:01.549
Fifty times the standard rate? Well, what kind of work would I be doing?

55
06:01.632 --> 06:04.469
Um, I don't have any special skills, but I've done plenty of temp gigs.

56
06:04.552 --> 06:07.805
Sign holding, bathhouse cleaning, PC bangs, deliveries,

57
06:07.889 --> 06:09.432
dishwashing, selling fish.

58
06:09.515 --> 06:10.933
Oh, and ever since I was a kid,

59
06:11.017 --> 06:13.227
once I start something, I see it through to the end--

60
06:13.311 --> 06:14.437
It's a convenience store.

61
06:16.939 --> 06:19.942
Wait a second. What? The job's at a store?

62
06:20.026 --> 06:21.861
Nothing you'll need to prepare, Hyeok-jun.

63
06:21.944 --> 06:24.572
Just tell them everything when you get there.

64
06:26.574 --> 06:27.909
Oh, okay.

65
06:30.786 --> 06:33.247
You just said my name. How'd you know?

66
06:34.499 --> 06:35.666
Oh.

67
06:36.417 --> 06:37.710
Tell me your name, would you?

68
06:39.587 --> 06:41.964
Well, um, Byeon Hyeok-jun. You got it right.

69
06:42.048 --> 06:44.342
- You're 30, is that right? - I'm 30 years old, yeah.

70
06:44.425 --> 06:45.968
Thirty years old.

71
06:47.303 --> 06:49.805
WELCOME - SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

72
06:49.889 --> 06:52.016
Take a photo of your ID and send it to that number.

73
06:52.099 --> 06:55.394
And I don't need any of your banking info. We only deal in cash.

74
06:55.478 --> 06:57.063
Oh, uh… Uh…

75
06:57.146 --> 06:59.982
You had my phone number, but I never gave it to you.

76
07:02.276 --> 07:04.237
Oh. Didn't you call ahead of time?

77
07:05.112 --> 07:07.740
I didn't call. I saw an ad under the Hangang Bridge.

78
07:09.033 --> 07:10.034
Uh-huh.

79
07:11.202 --> 07:13.996
The Hangang, yeah. That's right.

80
07:15.665 --> 07:17.583
Hangang Bridge is a classic.

81
07:20.962 --> 07:23.005
ENTER CONVENIENCE STORE, NIGHT SHIFT 10 P.M. - 6 A.M.

82
07:23.089 --> 07:26.050
- Eight hours at 50 times-- - It's four million won, give or take.

83
07:29.720 --> 07:32.265
You want the job, you just reply by text to accept it.

84
07:33.224 --> 07:36.477
- I just text "accept?" Yes. Accept. - Oh, hold on.

85
07:37.353 --> 07:39.981
You accept the terms, and you can't back out.

86
07:41.983 --> 07:45.695
If you're absent with no notice, we'll charge you a full day's wages as penalty.

87
07:47.280 --> 07:50.116
- I would be the one to pay? - And just one more thing.

88
07:51.492 --> 07:53.744
If at any time while you're working this gig

89
07:53.828 --> 07:56.038
you disclose what happens on the job to any third party,

90
07:56.122 --> 07:57.957
you will be incurring a penalty.

91
08:03.421 --> 08:05.464
Make it through one day, okay?

92
08:05.965 --> 08:07.383
Go make some cash.

93
08:10.386 --> 08:11.220
Oh.

94
08:12.179 --> 08:13.139
Blood?

95
08:26.694 --> 08:28.362
Oh. I… I'm sorry.

96
08:28.946 --> 08:29.989
So sorry!

97
08:31.741 --> 08:33.200
I… I'll just come back later.

98
08:38.414 --> 08:39.790
So much money.

99
08:40.291 --> 08:42.918
But I can't. Not even for 50 times. No, no, no.

100
08:47.923 --> 08:51.844
Well, look who it is! Long time, no see!

101
08:55.640 --> 08:57.391
Hey, Hyeok-jun.

102
08:57.475 --> 08:58.643
Du-jong.

103
08:58.726 --> 09:00.770
Come with me. I need to get some meat!

104
09:02.897 --> 09:04.065
You little shit.

105
09:04.148 --> 09:06.901
You came crying to me about how you got scammed out of your mom's money

106
09:06.984 --> 09:08.778
on some fucked-up lease.

107
09:09.904 --> 09:13.032
And how low did I make the interest rate on the money I leant you?

108
09:13.532 --> 09:17.119
Huh? You can't pay back what you owe me, so you just ghost me instead?

109
09:17.203 --> 09:20.039
I wanted to pay you what I owed, so I bought some stocks like you told--

110
09:20.122 --> 09:23.876
Seriously? Fucking asshole! Do you have a death wish or something?

111
09:24.377 --> 09:26.629
Oh.

112
09:26.712 --> 09:29.548
You little shit. So, it's my fault now?

113
09:29.632 --> 09:30.758
Really?

114
09:31.258 --> 09:32.259
Du-jong…

115
09:36.555 --> 09:38.766
Guess I fucked up bad, didn't I?

116
09:38.849 --> 09:41.894
There's a way out. Just don't give up like a coward. Do as I say.

117
09:41.977 --> 09:44.522
Here. Drink this.

118
09:45.106 --> 09:48.359
Your body probably needs some help. It needs work.

119
09:48.442 --> 09:50.695
What? My body?

120
09:53.114 --> 09:55.199
It's just the world we're in.

121
09:57.368 --> 10:01.288
This client of mine, out of nowhere, started paying off massive debts.

122
10:01.789 --> 10:03.666
And apparently, he does webcam videos.

123
10:03.749 --> 10:05.668
I was like, "Whoa, brilliant!"

124
10:06.168 --> 10:08.546
Why the fuck didn't I think of a move like that?

125
10:10.047 --> 10:13.884
My bro said that he's just raking in cash on all these freaky sites.

126
10:15.261 --> 10:17.096
So, get your body in shape, dumbass.

127
10:17.179 --> 10:20.349
You've got interest to pay tomorrow. Four million won.

128
10:20.433 --> 10:23.102
And if you don't pay, you'll get slapped with 10% late fees.

129
10:34.947 --> 10:38.534
Byeon Hyeok-jun, I'm saying this just in case I need to.

130
10:39.326 --> 10:42.663
Don't even start to consider running away or committing suicide.

131
10:45.416 --> 10:47.668
Because if a guy like you dies,

132
10:47.752 --> 10:50.212
and then your family tries ignoring the debt that you left?

133
10:51.172 --> 10:53.424
Man, we would never, ever let that go.

134
10:53.507 --> 10:56.802
I mean, we've got to make a living too. Got it?

135
10:57.303 --> 10:59.680
Nothing's scarier than other people's money.

136
11:10.983 --> 11:12.610
CONVENIENCE STORE NIGHT SHIFT

137
11:17.782 --> 11:20.534
ACCEPT

138
11:22.787 --> 11:24.997
ACCEPT

139
11:44.058 --> 11:47.269
How hard could a convenience store temp job possibly be?

140
11:59.323 --> 12:01.992
ENTER CONVENIENCE STORE NIGHT SHIFT 50 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE

141
12:02.076 --> 12:04.662
STARTS AT 10 P.M. ENDS AT 6 A.M.

142
12:23.180 --> 12:25.808
"Convenience store operating rules?"

143
12:35.276 --> 12:39.321
"Do not enter the storage room if you hear any noises inside."

144
12:41.240 --> 12:45.619
"Use the cross in the storage room to deal with non-human entities"?

145
12:47.705 --> 12:48.914
STORAGE ROOM

146
12:48.998 --> 12:50.708
There's a cross in there?

147
12:51.959 --> 12:54.670
CONVENIENCE STORE RULES WORK IN PAIRS

148
12:54.753 --> 12:56.672
RULE VIOLATIONS RESULT IN PENALTIES

149
12:56.755 --> 12:58.507
ANY NOISES INSIDE THE STORAGE ROOM

150
12:58.591 --> 13:00.509
COMPLETE INVENTORY

151
13:05.180 --> 13:06.515
Yes, Mr. Hyeok-jun?

152
13:06.599 --> 13:07.933
Oh, yeah, hello.

153
13:08.017 --> 13:10.436
I'm just calling to ask if this gig is

154
13:10.978 --> 13:15.190
maybe… maybe some prank video that someone's filming with a hidden camera?

155
13:16.775 --> 13:20.529
No, it's not. If that were the case, I'd have notified you in advance.

156
13:20.613 --> 13:21.614
What's the matter?

157
13:22.197 --> 13:24.325
Well, um, there's this rulebook for the job,

158
13:24.408 --> 13:26.368
and I'm kinda freaked out by what it says.

159
13:27.036 --> 13:30.039
Oh, and it says that there should be two of us, but now it's just me here.

160
13:30.122 --> 13:31.373
Anyone else in here?

161
13:33.834 --> 13:34.919
Mr. Hyeok-jun…

162
13:37.338 --> 13:39.423
if this were just an ordinary convenience store,

163
13:39.506 --> 13:42.593
do you really think we'd pay you 50 times the minimum wage?

164
13:43.218 --> 13:46.180
And just think, what would happen if you quit?

165
13:46.972 --> 13:49.767
Are you going to go back to the Hangang Bridge?

166
13:51.393 --> 13:54.146
All you need to do is hold on for eight hours.

167
13:54.813 --> 13:56.065
Give it some thought.

168
14:03.447 --> 14:05.282
"Last-minute second chance?"

169
14:07.242 --> 14:08.243
Let's go.

170
14:09.119 --> 14:10.371
Get it together.

171
14:15.459 --> 14:17.836
DO NOT ENTER THE STORAGE ROOM IF YOU HEAR ANY NOISES INSIDE

172
14:17.920 --> 14:19.463
Hello there, everyone!

173
14:19.546 --> 14:23.092
Your financial fairy godmother is back to tell you what stocks are hot.

174
14:23.175 --> 14:25.761
The biotech stock crash aftershocks just continue.

175
14:25.844 --> 14:28.013
Especially for Jeda Bio. This bad investment…

176
14:28.097 --> 14:30.683
God, I'm such an idiot. Why did I buy that stock?

177
14:31.767 --> 14:34.186
…classic example of a stock that was doomed to fail,

178
14:34.269 --> 14:36.271
no matter what some financial gurus said.

179
14:36.355 --> 14:38.941
Are you gonna take their word for it and throw away the money…

180
14:47.241 --> 14:48.951
How did this get down here?

181
15:01.672 --> 15:03.048
Who's doing that?

182
15:09.346 --> 15:11.890
Why is everything falling? It's not like they're stocks.

183
15:14.143 --> 15:15.853
Oh, shit!

184
15:21.900 --> 15:23.277
Fuck this!

185
15:28.615 --> 15:30.826
Why is it locked? Come on, open!

186
15:43.714 --> 15:47.718
Turn on, turn on! No, no, no, no! Oh God!

187
15:47.801 --> 15:48.844
Uh…

188
16:24.588 --> 16:25.964
Wait a minute. Is there somebody--

189
16:26.048 --> 16:27.299
Oh, shit!

190
16:27.966 --> 16:29.927
Excuse me.

191
16:30.844 --> 16:32.054
Hey, you good?

192
16:35.265 --> 16:36.308
Oh, uh, yeah.

193
16:36.391 --> 16:38.894
Uh, can I come inside?

194
16:42.481 --> 16:44.316
Sure. Okay.

195
16:47.653 --> 16:48.904
That's a yes, right?

196
16:51.698 --> 16:54.076
I'm sorry. I… I may have overreacted.

197
16:54.159 --> 16:57.246
Tonight's my first night shift, so I guess I'm seeing things.

198
16:57.329 --> 16:59.123
Oh, so it's also new for you?

199
16:59.832 --> 17:00.999
Totally. Same here.

200
17:02.376 --> 17:05.629
What do you mean? You're seeing stuff too?

201
17:06.130 --> 17:07.381
Bro, I meant the gig.

202
17:08.465 --> 17:11.009
NIGHT SHIFT WORKERS MUST WORK IN PAIRS UNAUTHORIZED DEPARTURE IS PROHIBITED

203
17:11.677 --> 17:15.139
Oh, this uniform's sick. And it's the perfect size.

204
17:16.765 --> 17:19.226
Why would you get here two hours after we had to start?

205
17:19.726 --> 17:21.728
Sorry, man. Choi Hee-dong's the name.

206
17:22.563 --> 17:23.605
Turned 21 this year.

207
17:23.689 --> 17:24.731
You're 21?

208
17:26.692 --> 17:28.610
What's your excuse for coming so late?

209
17:28.694 --> 17:31.572
I was doing everything by myself! I was here all alone.

210
17:31.655 --> 17:32.948
Calm down.

211
17:33.448 --> 17:36.743
Don't get so pissed off. Let me handle the rest of the hard stuff.

212
17:37.536 --> 17:38.662
You don't get it.

213
17:38.745 --> 17:41.999
Earlier, I, like, jumped out of my skin. It's scary.

214
17:42.082 --> 17:44.001
- This job is really-- - The job is what?

215
17:44.501 --> 17:47.171
There's just something s… s… spooky about all this.

216
17:51.425 --> 17:53.010
What's spooky about it?

217
17:57.472 --> 18:03.020
"Complete inspection within five minutes after noises in the storage room stop?"

218
18:04.479 --> 18:06.690
- The fuck is this? - Wanna know what's crazy?

219
18:07.191 --> 18:08.984
I don't think any of this is a joke.

220
18:09.776 --> 18:13.113
Ever since the moment I got here, no one's come in except for you.

221
18:13.614 --> 18:16.366
Also, I mean, weird things just keep happening.

222
18:19.328 --> 18:20.746
What are you talking about?

223
18:27.544 --> 18:31.381
Oh my God! This! Here it goes. Listen. Do you hear that? I'm not crazy, right?

224
18:34.843 --> 18:37.429
What is that? It's really freaking me out.

225
18:38.222 --> 18:39.765
Maybe it's a ghost!

226
18:40.891 --> 18:42.351
Who knows? It's creeping me out.

227
18:42.434 --> 18:45.520
What on Earth would even be able to make a sound that horrifying?

228
18:46.939 --> 18:48.482
God, I'm so into this.

229
18:48.982 --> 18:51.318
Wh… What?

230
18:52.361 --> 18:53.654
I'm obsessed with horror.

231
18:53.737 --> 18:56.990
I watch so many horror channels. I'm subscribed to every one. It's true.

232
18:57.074 --> 19:00.911
Well, if you like horror so much, maybe you should go.

233
19:00.994 --> 19:02.704
Do the inspection yourself.

234
19:03.372 --> 19:06.041
I mean, I would, but the thing about the inspection is

235
19:07.000 --> 19:08.710
I'm not even sure how to do it.

236
19:15.634 --> 19:18.553
- What do you mean? - This is the first temp job I've ever had.

237
19:19.054 --> 19:20.389
I'm new to all this.

238
19:21.431 --> 19:23.475
Why would anyone even hire you for this gig?

239
19:23.558 --> 19:25.519
They hired me for a pretty good reason.

240
19:26.436 --> 19:28.105
I have legendary mopping skills.

241
19:28.188 --> 19:32.651
When I was in the army, I earned extra leave for my mopping abilities. Yes, sir!

242
19:33.735 --> 19:36.280
Oh shit, it's my other hand. Yes, sir!

243
19:37.531 --> 19:39.408
Whoa. The weird noise stopped.

244
19:41.159 --> 19:43.537
I'll go check it out. Hurry up and mop the floor.

245
19:43.620 --> 19:45.330
Sure. Got it, bro.

246
19:48.625 --> 19:53.046
COMPLETE INVENTORY WITHIN FIVE MINUTES AFTER NOISES IN THE STORAGE ROOM STOP

247
20:02.848 --> 20:03.890
Oh, shit.

248
20:12.983 --> 20:17.279
Man, it's so dark in here. How am I supposed to do the inspection like this?

249
20:17.904 --> 20:19.448
This is bullshit.

250
20:30.542 --> 20:33.253
God, this computer looks ancient. How do I even do this?

251
20:34.504 --> 20:37.049
Oh, come on! Faster, faster. I don't have time.

252
20:38.633 --> 20:40.385
One fresh cream strawberry sandwich.

253
20:40.469 --> 20:43.180
Why aren't the keys working? Seriously?

254
20:49.269 --> 20:50.645
Faster. Come on, hurry up.

255
20:52.230 --> 20:56.443
Okay, so we have one of these. We've got two of these. Three of this one.

256
20:59.988 --> 21:02.199
Almost done, almost done. Come on, last one.

257
21:06.119 --> 21:07.412
That's it. I'm done.

258
21:12.584 --> 21:13.543
Damn it.

259
21:48.662 --> 21:49.913
You're already done?

260
21:51.289 --> 21:54.126
Some… some… something is in there, but I'm not sure what.

261
21:54.209 --> 21:55.293
What happened?

262
21:55.377 --> 21:57.379
I just… I don't even know! There's someone…

263
21:57.462 --> 22:01.133
But no. No, no. Maybe not someone, but some thing in there.

264
22:01.216 --> 22:03.009
It was like a person. No, it wasn't a person--

265
22:03.093 --> 22:04.177
What are you talking about?

266
22:04.261 --> 22:06.430
There's a thing inside the fridge with a human face,

267
22:06.513 --> 22:08.265
but that thing was not human.

268
22:08.348 --> 22:10.350
Its body was like a bug or something!

269
22:10.434 --> 22:12.018
The body is like a fucking bug?

270
22:12.102 --> 22:13.895
A human face…

271
22:14.396 --> 22:16.565
- No, no. This is crazy. - The body of a bug?

272
22:16.648 --> 22:19.568
I've got… I've got to get some sleep. That's what going on.

273
22:19.651 --> 22:22.821
No, wait. Is it a doll in there, maybe? Is this a prank show or something?

274
22:22.904 --> 22:25.449
Hee-dong, look for cameras. This has to be a prank.

275
22:26.241 --> 22:27.242
No, no, no, wait.

276
22:28.535 --> 22:30.287
I don't think it's a prank at all.

277
22:32.706 --> 22:33.915
It's a curse.

278
22:36.751 --> 22:38.170
It's The Curse of the Chimera.

279
22:38.253 --> 22:39.921
This horror channel made a video on it.

280
22:40.005 --> 22:42.299
Some creatures get their bodies mixed up together.

281
22:42.382 --> 22:45.594
Like, imagine you mixed with a flea and some parrot.

282
22:45.677 --> 22:47.220
Then that's you, bro.

283
22:49.264 --> 22:50.432
It's real, bro.

284
22:57.481 --> 22:58.982
I'm gonna get you!

285
22:59.065 --> 23:00.400
Comer on, man!

286
23:01.276 --> 23:04.738
Hey, stop it! Are you some kind of maniac or what? Seriously!

287
23:04.821 --> 23:07.032
- How are you not freaking right now? - Bro.

288
23:07.115 --> 23:09.993
Do you know how many ghosts are in the world nowadays?

289
23:10.535 --> 23:12.704
One's behind you right now!

290
23:15.790 --> 23:17.876
Bro, come on. I'm obviously just messing with you.

291
23:17.959 --> 23:20.045
"Agh!" You freaked me out.

292
23:24.007 --> 23:25.842
Go in there and see for yourself.

293
23:30.597 --> 23:31.556
Bro.

294
23:35.227 --> 23:36.978
In a situation like this,

295
23:37.604 --> 23:39.856
if it happened on a crazy horror channel--

296
23:39.940 --> 23:41.149
What?

297
23:41.233 --> 23:43.443
We'd learn all of this was the branch manager's doing.

298
23:44.027 --> 23:45.946
Maybe they wrote these ominous warnings

299
23:46.029 --> 23:48.073
to make it seem like there's a ghost as a red herring…

300
23:50.116 --> 23:52.994
to cover up a girl they kidnapped and locked in the storage room.

301
23:54.788 --> 23:56.623
It would be insane if that was true.

302
23:57.999 --> 23:59.709
I didn't say it's a girl in there.

303
24:00.460 --> 24:01.628
What?

304
24:01.711 --> 24:03.713
Oh, uh, it's nothing.

305
24:04.214 --> 24:06.758
Why do you keep acting so moody and mysterious?

306
24:08.677 --> 24:10.136
I should get back to work.

307
24:13.765 --> 24:15.100
CONVENIENCE STORE RULES

308
24:21.565 --> 24:22.440
What?

309
24:23.191 --> 24:24.859
"The second temp worker

310
24:25.443 --> 24:26.861
is not human."

311
24:32.576 --> 24:34.286
I'm gonna get you!

312
24:34.369 --> 24:37.080
God, I'm so into this. Oh, shit, it's my other hand. Yes, sir!

313
24:37.163 --> 24:39.541
Uh… can I come inside?

314
24:46.506 --> 24:50.760
USE THE CROSS IN THE STORAGE ROOM TO DEAL WITH NON-HUMAN ENTITIES

315
25:02.981 --> 25:08.862
USE THE CROSS IN THE STORAGE ROOM TO DEAL WITH NON-HUMAN ENTITIES

316
25:08.945 --> 25:11.323
- Ugh, come on, dude! - The count on these is off.

317
25:11.406 --> 25:13.700
Customers won't care about that. There's nobody here!

318
25:13.783 --> 25:15.327
I think I must have made a mistake

319
25:15.410 --> 25:17.871
when I was doing the storage room inspection.

320
25:17.954 --> 25:19.039
I should go do it again.

321
25:19.914 --> 25:20.999
I need to go back in.

322
25:21.082 --> 25:23.752
It's so creepy. Are you seriously going back in there?

323
25:25.670 --> 25:27.464
Just tell me what needs to be done.

324
25:29.049 --> 25:30.258
I'll go do it.

325
25:30.967 --> 25:33.762
No, no, don't worry. You said you've never done it, so--

326
25:33.845 --> 25:34.929
Come on, man.

327
25:37.557 --> 25:39.267
You're too nice a guy.

328
25:39.351 --> 25:42.103
You'll lose out on a lot if you live like that.

329
25:47.150 --> 25:48.693
Ha!

330
25:57.994 --> 25:59.913
Oh, shit.

331
25:59.996 --> 26:01.915
A cross. The cross. But… But where?

332
26:03.625 --> 26:04.459
The cross.

333
26:14.844 --> 26:17.138
Oh, whoa, what? What now?

334
26:21.351 --> 26:22.560
So, uh…

335
26:23.061 --> 26:26.481
Well, the bad person is probably my co-worker out there.

336
26:26.564 --> 26:28.274
The one outside? This will take him out?

337
26:34.447 --> 26:35.615
Am I right or not?

338
26:59.723 --> 27:00.765
Hey!

339
27:01.558 --> 27:02.976
You… You…

340
27:04.978 --> 27:07.439
I don't know what you are, but you better get out!

341
27:10.191 --> 27:12.861
I need to finish this crazy job and get paid!

342
27:28.209 --> 27:29.753
Agh!

343
27:40.388 --> 27:41.765
Oh, fuck!

344
28:10.251 --> 28:13.379
Where are you going? Oh, you want the cross?

345
28:20.637 --> 28:23.431
- No, get off! Why are you doing this? - Why do you think?

346
28:23.515 --> 28:25.517
This place was not made for two entities.

347
28:26.267 --> 28:29.646
What convenience store would hire two temps? One needs to go.

348
28:32.649 --> 28:34.234
Time for you to clock out

349
28:34.317 --> 28:35.610
of life.

350
28:44.619 --> 28:46.079
Oh!

351
28:58.341 --> 28:59.634
It doesn't work.

352
29:03.346 --> 29:06.266
That list of rules? I wrote every single one.

353
29:06.349 --> 29:09.936
You fucking idiot. You really believed those?

354
29:10.937 --> 29:12.939
I bullshitted it all.

355
29:13.022 --> 29:14.232
Wait, what?

356
29:14.315 --> 29:16.860
I fooled you. Okay, dumbass?

357
29:19.279 --> 29:21.573
Get away from me! Don't come any closer!

358
29:21.656 --> 29:22.949
Think you can run?

359
30:35.730 --> 30:36.940
Oh!

360
30:49.452 --> 30:50.870
Ah!

361
32:05.778 --> 32:07.488
Just like when I was a kid,

362
32:08.281 --> 32:10.950
I need to always see things through to the end.

363
32:29.969 --> 32:31.971
Oh, oh, oh!

364
34:21.664 --> 34:23.666
Huh?

365
35:12.089 --> 35:13.633
ALARM

366
35:13.716 --> 35:14.926
Six o'clock.

367
35:23.017 --> 35:25.937
PART-TIME JOB COMPLETED 4,012,000 WON

368
36:48.060 --> 36:50.187
The next one gets here soon.

369
36:50.271 --> 36:52.106
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY BOSS

370
36:55.192 --> 36:56.235
Hey, yeah?

371
36:56.319 --> 36:57.987
Byeon Hyeok-jun, hello.

372
36:58.487 --> 37:02.533
You completed the job successfully. You got a knack for this.

373
37:03.034 --> 37:04.702
So, I did work last night?

374
37:05.619 --> 37:07.163
It felt more like a bad nightmare.

375
37:07.246 --> 37:09.874
What, you think it was a nightmare?

376
37:09.957 --> 37:13.127
It was just a little temp job. It was a really easy gig, by the way.

377
37:14.378 --> 37:15.379
So, uh,

378
37:17.131 --> 37:18.883
are all the gigs like this?

379
37:20.259 --> 37:23.346
Well, you got it done. Isn't that the most important thing?

380
37:24.305 --> 37:26.682
And you made a lot of money, didn't you?

381
37:27.683 --> 37:28.851
So, when are you coming back?

382
37:28.934 --> 37:30.770
Soon. Soon, but, uh…

383
37:33.189 --> 37:35.358
Well, come and get your money when you can.

384
37:35.858 --> 37:37.193
I'll have it ready for you.

385
37:47.536 --> 37:50.373
KYUNGIL GROUP NEO WORLD

386
38:05.721 --> 38:09.225
RESIDENT REGISTRATION CARD

387
38:11.602 --> 38:13.270
"Byeon Hyeok-jun."

388
38:18.984 --> 38:21.070
I think we'll see each other again soon.

389
42:30.069 --> 42:31.862
ALL NAMES, EVENTS, BRANDS, PERSONS, AND PLACES

390
42:31.945 --> 42:33.530
DEPICTED IN THIS SERIES ARE FICTIONAL

391
42:33.614 --> 42:35.532
ANY RESEMBLANCE TO REALITY IS COINCIDENTAL
